<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Synod of Whitby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">664</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Synod of Whitby was a church council held in 664 at the abbey of Whitby, presided over by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu of Northumbria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfrid">Wilfrid</a> argued for Roman practice and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Colmán for the Irish tradition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iona">Iona</a> in calculating the date of Easter; Oswiu chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Colmán withdrew to Iona, and the English church moved closer to Rome.</p></div>
